  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 400 AM MDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nEnsembles are in fairly good agreement showing PW peaking on Tuesday \nacross the area with the latest monsoon surge. Rainfall chances will \nremain elevated as the powerful ridge recedes ever so slightly. \nWhile we are not expecting temperatures to fall below average, we \nshould see the heat ease to slightly more reasonable values only \nabout 5F above seasonal norms by Tuesday. This will be the theme for \nmuch of the weak beyond Tuesday as 700-mb temperatures remain \ngenerally in the +16 to +19C range. On the synoptic scale, the \npowerful ridge will begin to retrograde westward and also broaden \nits horizontal extent. The result of this is a reduction in the \nquality of the monsoon moisture plume as the week progresses. \nRecycled moisture trapped underneath the ridge will continue to \nproduce daily chances for showers and thunderstorms Wednesday \nonwards, but expect PW to decrease gradually each day with a little \nlower overall thunderstorm coverage.",
